--- HTTP/1.1 reuses the connection by default
requests served -> 2
nothing left unread -> b''
--- two requests, one connection
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 7'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/first\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 8'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/second\n'
--- HTTP/1.0 does not, unless it asks
requests served -> 1
the second request was never read -> b'GET /second HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n'
--- 1.0 closes after one
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 7'
    b'connection: close'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/first\n'
1.0 with Connection: keep-alive -> 2
--- 1.0 kept alive is told so
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 7'
    b'connection: keep-alive'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/first\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 8'
    b'connection: keep-alive'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/second\n'
--- Connection: close ends it from either side
the client asked to close -> 1
a comma list is read as a list -> 1
the handler asked to close -> 1
--- an unread request body is drained, not left to be parsed as a request
requests served -> 2
--- the body was skipped, not parsed
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 9'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/ignored\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 8'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'/second\n'
--- a body too large to be worth draining closes the connection instead
requests served -> 1
the response says the connection is ending -> True
--- a connection cannot be reused forever
requests served before the cap -> 1000
the last response says the connection is ending -> True
--- a handler that raises is a 500, and says so on stderr
http: handler raised <class 'ValueError'>: a bug in the handler, not in the request
requests served -> 1
--- 500 response
    b'HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 22'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'internal server error\n'
--- a handler that builds a header out of user input cannot inject one
http: handler raised <class 'ValueError'>: illegal character in response header value for 'x-echo'
--- 500, not an injected header
    b'HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 22'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'internal server error\n'
--- a body that cannot be drained closes the connection rather than escaping
requests served -> 1
--- answered, then closed
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 22'
    b'connection: close'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'did not read the body\n'
--- a handler that raises BadRequest is answered as the client error it is
--- 422 response
    b'HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Content'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 19'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'your JSON is wrong\n'
--- a malformed request is answered and the connection ends
requests served -> 0
the second request was never read -> b'GET /second HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\n\r\n'
--- 400 response
    b'HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 39'
    b'connection: close'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b'HTTP/1.1 request without a Host header\n'
--- routing
an exact route -> 200 allow=- b'ok\n'
a parameterised route binds its segment -> 200 allow=- b'42\n'
a different method on the same path -> 201 allow=- b'created\n'
no route at all -> 404 allow=- b'not found\n'
a known path, a wrong method -> 405 allow=GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
a known pattern, a wrong method -> 405 allow=GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
HEAD is served by the GET route -> 200 allow=- b'ok\n'
an empty segment does not bind a parameter -> 404 allow=- b'not found\n'
--- and HEAD's body is dropped on the way out, not by the route
--- HEAD /health
    b'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'
    b'content-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8'
    b'content-length: 3'
    b'date: <clock>'
    b''
    b''
